From 48893a71372d47285506eb0c621d3aae82ba9fd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AUTH-01 Native Convergence <auth01-agent@local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 02:18:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] test(auth): complete buyer RPC security certification

Add docs/auth01-rpc-security-matrix.md: the complete 36/36 body-verified
Buyer RPC security matrix for AUTH-01, closing the evidence gap from the
prior certification commit (93ca72a), which had only 9/36 RPCs body-read
and the rest grant-verified only.

All 36 entries in buyer-deployment-rpc-allowlist.ts / verify-contract-
boundary.mjs are now individually classified (PUBLIC SAFE / PRE-LOGIN
PUBLIC INTAKE / AUTHENTICATED BUYER / BUYER + STAFF / INTERNAL ONLY) with
direct evidence: exact migration file, company-derivation mechanism,
cross-company protection, and frozen/inactive handling for each.

Two real Core defects were found during this body audit and fixed on a
separate Core branch (auth01-rpc-staff-exclusion-fix, not this repo):

- customer_order_status_v1 / customer_order_items_v1 /
  customer_support_tickets_v1 used an inline eligibility gate with no role
  filter and no staff exclusion, unlike the canonical
  customer_buyer_eligible_company_id() helper introduced later for exactly
  this family. Core commit 8a81780 fixes all three to call the canonical
  helper, plus a pgTAP regression (not run -- no live Postgres in this
  sandbox).
- get_sales_order_pi_final_payment_request_v1 and its three governing RLS
  policies used the weaker auth_buyer_company_id() helper (no
  approved/status/frozen check), letting a buyer whose company was later
  frozen still read final-payment-PI details for their own orders. Core
  commit 5de4246 fixes this using the same canonical-helper swap, plus a
  pgTAP regression (also not run).

A third, lower-severity occurrence of the identical drift (in the
support_ticket_set_customer_context() BEFORE INSERT trigger that actually
governs submit_customer_support_ticket_v1's authorization) was found and
documented but NOT fixed -- it's a write-path attribution edge case, not a
data-disclosure defect (order-ownership is independently and correctly
enforced by the same trigger), and warrants its own careful pass rather
than a rushed edit to a trigger with several unrelated field resets.
Recorded as a follow-up recommendation in the matrix doc, along with a
second open item: create_payment_gateway_payable_intent_v1 and
get_payment_gateway_payable_status_v1 use the same auth_buyer_company_id()
helper that was fixed for final-payment-PI, and were not independently
re-verified/fixed in this pass.

No native app code changed in this commit -- this is documentation of the
already-complete AUTH-01 implementation (0d22600, 4b96419, 93ca72a).

Verified: npm run quality still passes end to end (unchanged from the
prior commit -- 160/160 tests, typecheck, lint, boundary/rc-scan/
rc-navigation/cert:bindings/census:p106/expo-config all clean). No
production mutation of any kind, in either repository.
